   "claims": [
    "Tire 1: / R Tire 2: / R Tire code Car tires are described by an alphanumeric code, as shown in the figure below.",
    "Intended use: The first part of the code is made up of 1 or 2 letters (P, LT, ST, T) that describe the type of vehicle that the tire is intended to be used with.",
    "Nominal section width: The second part of the code is a 3-digit number that describes the nominal section width of the tire in millimeters (mm).",
    "In the figure above, the 215 means that the nominal section width of the tire is 215 mm.",
    "It is a 2- or 3-digit number that indicates the ratio of the tire's section height to its width.",
    "A tire with the code xxx/65 indicates that the section height of the tire is 65% of its width.",
    "For example, for a tire with code 200/65, the section height is 200 × 65% = 130 mm.",
    "Cross-ply tires are tires whose internal construction is made of nylon cord placed diagonally across each other, usually at an angle of 55°.",
    "Diameter of the wheel: The next part of the code is a 1- or 2-digit number that indicates the diameter of the wheel, in units of inches, that the tire is designed to fit.",
    "Load index: The next part of the code is a 2- or 3-digit number referred to as the load index of the tire."
   ],
